				<r3d:description language="eng">The University of Opole Knowledge Base is the central institutional system for recording, archiving, and disseminating the scholarly, artistic, and educational outputs of the University of Opole community. It includes a repository that stores publications, doctoral theses, patents, artistic works, and — upon author request — open research data. Deposited content is made available under Creative Commons licenses (CC BY-NC), unless restrictions apply due to licensing, patents, or grant conditions.

The repository supports the FAIR principles of research data management and is indexed in OpenAIRE, ensuring international visibility and interoperability. It is also registered in the EOSC Resource Hub and in OpenDOAR, and provides persistent identifiers (DOI) via DataCite.

Repository content:
- Scholarly publications (articles, monographs, book chapters)
- Doctoral theses (mandatory deposit)
- Patents and artistic works
- Open research data (raw and processed), with metadata, abstracts, and keywords in Polish and English</r3d:description>
